  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b000001",
      "kind": "quote",
      "start_line": 1,
      "end_line": 1,
      "raw": "> Historical iiHtmlBlock documentation, preserved after integration into iiXml. Current build and package instructions are in [HTML block integration](../HtmlBlockIntegration.md).\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000002",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 2,
      "end_line": 2,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000003",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 3,
      "end_line": 3,
      "raw": "# iiHtmlBlock\n",
      "level": 1,
      "title": "iiHtmlBlock"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000004",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 4,
      "end_line": 4,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 5,
      "end_line": 5,
      "raw": "[Windows build and execution](WindowsBuildAndRun.md)\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000006",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 6,
      "end_line": 6,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 7,
      "end_line": 9,
      "raw": "Package release: **0.1.1** (2026-10-19). This patch packages the current\nsource snapshot; build, test and installation evidence is recorded in the SDK\npatch-release report. Earlier versioned feature notes remain historical.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000008",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 10,
      "end_line": 11,
      "raw": "\n\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 12,
      "end_line": 12,
      "raw": "`iiHtmlBlock` is a Qt6.8.3/C++20 shared library for converting `iiXml` input into HTML blocks and manipulating them. The public C++ API resides under the `iiHtmlBlock` namespace.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000010",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 13,
      "end_line": 13,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000011",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 14,
      "end_line": 14,
      "raw": "## GetTagInfo\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "GetTagInfo"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000012",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 15,
      "end_line": 15,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000013",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 16,
      "end_line": 16,
      "raw": "`Src/Parser/GetTagInfo.*` accepts an XML string and stores the first root tag's value and fields as internal state in a way compatible with `iiXml::Parser::TagParser`. The full tag hierarchy is queried through `GetTags()`/`GetRoot()`, while the first root tag's value and fields are queried through `GetValue()` and `GetFields()`. iiXml structures that are difficult to represent with a tree alone, such as crossing closing tags, are preserved as the original offset ranges in `GetRanges()`. The XML declaration and DOCTYPE preceding the body tags are not tag ranges and are therefore removed before parsing.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000014",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 17,
      "end_line": 17,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000015",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 18,
      "end_line": 18,
      "raw": "See `get_tag_info.md` for details.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000016",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 19,
      "end_line": 19,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000017",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 20,
      "end_line": 20,
      "raw": "## GetHTML\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "GetHTML"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000018",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 21,
      "end_line": 21,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000019",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 22,
      "end_line": 22,
      "raw": "`Src/Parser/GetHTML.*` accepts `iiXml` and other XML strings and determines them as HTML tag strings. Tag names are not transformed, and tags like `paragraph`, `XML`, `CustomTag` are also returned as custom HTML tags with their original names. Unknown tags are also kept with their input names. For example, `unknownName` is returned as `<unknownName>...</unknownName>`, and `OtherWidget` is returned as `<OtherWidget>...</OtherWidget>`.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000020",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 23,
      "end_line": 23,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000021",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 24,
      "end_line": 24,
      "raw": "See `get_html.md` for details.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000022",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 25,
      "end_line": 25,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000023",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 26,
      "end_line": 26,
      "raw": "## iiXmlToHTML\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "iiXmlToHTML"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000024",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 27,
      "end_line": 27,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000025",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 28,
      "end_line": 28,
      "raw": "`Src/Modifier/iiXmlToHTML.*` uses the determination rules of `GetHTML` to transform iiXml / XML input into HTML string. Tag names are not transformed and are kept with their input names.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000026",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 29,
      "end_line": 29,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000027",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 30,
      "end_line": 30,
      "raw": "See `iixml_to_html.md` for details.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000028",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 31,
      "end_line": 31,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000029",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 32,
      "end_line": 32,
      "raw": "## DivideBlock\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "DivideBlock"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000030",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 33,
      "end_line": 33,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000031",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 34,
      "end_line": 34,
      "raw": "`Src/Modifier/DivideBlock.*` determines whether each element is a block unit based on the tag range parsed by `GetTagInfo`. It recognizes the default HTML block tag, and explicit display values like `style=\"display: block\"` or `display=block` take precedence over the default tag determination. Unknown custom tags are considered blocks only when an explicit display value exists.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000032",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 35,
      "end_line": 35,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000033",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 36,
      "end_line": 36,
      "raw": "See `divide_block.md` for details.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000034",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 37,
      "end_line": 37,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000035",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 38,
      "end_line": 38,
      "raw": "## BlockRangeTracker\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "BlockRangeTracker"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000036",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 39,
      "end_line": 39,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000037",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 40,
      "end_line": 40,
      "raw": "`Src/Modifier/BlockRangeTracker.*` tracks blocks determined by `DivideBlock` in units of the original text range. Each block is assigned a tracking ID, and a specific block can be looked up or blocks overlapping a given offset/range can be found based on the offset relative to the entire original text. `Update()` maintains existing block IDs when possible while reparsing the new document.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000038",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 41,
      "end_line": 41,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000039",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 42,
      "end_line": 42,
      "raw": "See `block_range_tracker.md` for details.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000040",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 43,
      "end_line": 43,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000041",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 44,
      "end_line": 44,
      "raw": "## BlockHTMLSerializer\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "BlockHTMLSerializer"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000042",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 45,
      "end_line": 45,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000043",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 46,
      "end_line": 46,
      "raw": "`Src/Modifier/BlockHTMLSerializer.*` serializes the split results of `DivideBlock` and the merge results of `CombineBlock` into HTML string fragments. Nested blocks are not duplicated; they are output only once as included in the parent block, and the merge results are used as logical block fragments `CombinedBlock::raw`.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000044",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 47,
      "end_line": 47,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000045",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 48,
      "end_line": 48,
      "raw": "See `block_html_serializer.md` for details.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000046",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 49,
      "end_line": 49,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000047",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 50,
      "end_line": 50,
      "raw": "## DeleteBlock\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "DeleteBlock"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000048",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 51,
      "end_line": 51,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000049",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 52,
      "end_line": 52,
      "raw": "`Src/Modifier/DeleteBlock.*` removes the specified block from the original HTML / iiXml string in the block list divided by `DivideBlock`. After deletion, the remaining document is reparsed to update the current block list, and the deleted block snapshot can be looked up at `GetDeletedBlocks()`.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000050",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 53,
      "end_line": 53,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000051",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 54,
      "end_line": 54,
      "raw": "See `delete_block.md` for details.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000052",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 55,
      "end_line": 55,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000053",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 56,
      "end_line": 56,
      "raw": "## CombineBlock\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "CombineBlock"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000054",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 57,
      "end_line": 57,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000055",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 58,
      "end_line": 58,
      "raw": "`Src/Modifier/CombineBlock.*` selects multiple blocks from the block list divided by `DivideBlock` and treats the selected group as a single logical block for merging. Merging saves the selection indices and the selected block snapshots to `CombinedBlock` without rewriting the original HTML.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000056",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 59,
      "end_line": 59,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000057",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 60,
      "end_line": 60,
      "raw": "See `combine_block.md` for details.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000058",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 61,
      "end_line": 61,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000059",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 62,
      "end_line": 62,
      "raw": "## FlattenBlock\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "FlattenBlock"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000060",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 63,
      "end_line": 63,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000061",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 64,
      "end_line": 64,
      "raw": "`Src/Modifier/FlattenBlock.*` groups all blocks of the document into a single parent group block layer while maintaining each block. Each block remains as an individual `ElementInfo` while simultaneously being treated as a block included in a single `LayerBlock` group.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000062",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 65,
      "end_line": 65,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000063",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 66,
      "end_line": 66,
      "raw": "See `flatten_block.md` for details.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000064",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 67,
      "end_line": 67,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000065",
      "kind": "html",
      "start_line": 68,
      "end_line": 68,
      "raw": "<a id=\"설치\"></a>\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000066",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 69,
      "end_line": 69,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000067",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 70,
      "end_line": 70,
      "raw": "## Install\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "Install"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000068",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 71,
      "end_line": 71,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000069",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 72,
      "end_line": 72,
      "raw": "`install.sh` builds, tests, and installs at once in the same manner as iiXml, and installs iiHtmlBlock as macOS, iOS, Android, WASM packages. The compatible root prefix for macOS is `~/.local/SDK/iiHtmlBlock`, and platform-specific packages are placed in `~/.local/SDK/iiHtmlBlock/platforms/<platform>`. After installation, the consuming project can separately add the `iiXml` prefix without using the standard install layout, or can directly import `find_package(iiHtmlBlock CONFIG REQUIRED)` or the install config file `include()`. The root config delegates to the platform package corresponding to the CMake target system to prevent the host dylib from being incorrectly linked in cross-compilation.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000070",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 73,
      "end_line": 73,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000071",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 74,
      "end_line": 74,
      "raw": "Targets specified by the consumer `iiXml_DIR` or already retrieved `iiXml::iiXml` are preserved. Automatic platform discovery is used only when there is no explicit selection, and XML packages using new iiFileProvider CRUD hierarchies are not reverted to the previous `.local` installation. `installed_dependency_selection_test` reads the actual installation package as a separate CMake consumer to verify that this selection is maintained.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000072",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 75,
      "end_line": 75,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000073",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 76,
      "end_line": 76,
      "raw": "See `install.md` for details.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000074",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 77,
      "end_line": 77,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000075",
      "kind": "html",
      "start_line": 78,
      "end_line": 78,
      "raw": "<a id=\"사용-예시\"></a>\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000076",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 79,
      "end_line": 79,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000077",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 80,
      "end_line": 80,
      "raw": "## Usage Examples\n",
      "level": 2,
      "title": "Usage Examples"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000078",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 81,
      "end_line": 81,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000079",
      "kind": "fenced_code",
      "start_line": 82,
      "end_line": 90,
      "raw": "```cpp\n#include <iiHtmlBlock>\n\niiHtmlBlock::GetHTML html;\niiHtmlBlock::DivideBlock divider;\niiHtmlBlock::BlockRangeTracker tracker;\niiHtmlBlock::BlockHTMLSerializer serializer;\niiHtmlBlock::DeleteBlock deleter;\n```\n",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "#include <iiHtmlBlock>\n\niiHtmlBlock::GetHTML html;\niiHtmlBlock::DivideBlock divider;\niiHtmlBlock::BlockRangeTracker tracker;\niiHtmlBlock::BlockHTMLSerializer serializer;\niiHtmlBlock::DeleteBlock deleter;\n",
      "closed": true
    },
    {
      "id": "b000080",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 91,
      "end_line": 91,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000081",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 92,
      "end_line": 92,
      "raw": "Runnable examples are in `Example/ParsedXmlHtmlExample.cpp`, and they show together the parsed XML range, HTML transformation results, block splitting, range tracking, block serialization, block deletion, selection merging, and the full layering flow. See `examples.md` for details.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000082",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 93,
      "end_line": 93,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000083",
      "kind": "html",
      "start_line": 94,
      "end_line": 94,
      "raw": "<a id=\"검증\"></a>\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000084",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 95,
      "end_line": 95,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
